{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTCornerListConnection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTCornerListConnection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTListCorner","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationFintype"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_filter_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_filter_eq","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L215-L223","doc":"**`numSYTenum` is invariant under removing trailing zeros** from a sorted shape — both count\nstandard fillings of the same Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.ofRowLens_filter_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.ofRowLens_filter_eq","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L205-L213","doc":"Filtering trailing zeros from a sorted shape leaves its Young diagram unchanged (a `0`-length row\ncontributes no cells). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerRecursion_proof","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerRecursion_proof","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L164-L203","doc":"**`cornerRecursion`, discharged.** `#SYT(λ) = ∑_{removable corners i} #SYT(removeCorner λ i)`,\nproved through the structural branching rule and the diagram↔list corner correspondence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_corners_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_corners_of","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L158-L162","doc":"A removable corner row index belongs to `corners l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eraseCorner_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eraseCorner_congr","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L153-L156","doc":"Corner removal depends only on the cell: equal corner cells give the same diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.num_eraseCorner_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.num_eraseCorner_eq","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**Per-corner summand equality.** The structural count of the corner-deleted diagram equals the\nbrute-force count of the list-level `removeCorner`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eq_cornerCell_of_isCornerCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eq_cornerCell_of_isCornerCell","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L132-L142","doc":"**A diagram corner is the last cell of its row.** Any removable corner `cell` of the diagram of `λ`\nequals `cornerCell λ (row)` — its column is `λ_row − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eraseCorner_ofRowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.eraseCorner_ofRowLens","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L110-L130","doc":"**The geometric heart.** Deleting the corner cell `(i, λ_i − 1)` from the diagram of `λ` gives the\ndiagram of `removeCorner λ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isCornerCell_ofRowLens_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isCornerCell_ofRowLens_iff","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L91-L108","doc":"**List corner ⇔ diagram corner.** Row index `i` is a removable corner of `λ` iff the cell\n`(i, λ_i − 1)` is a removable corner of the diagram of `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerCell","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The corner cell of row `i` is `(i, λ_i − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_ofRowLens_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_ofRowLens_iff","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L77-L86","doc":"Cell membership in `ofRowLens` via `getD`: `(r,c) ∈ ofRowLens w hw ↔ c < w_r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removeCorner_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removeCorner_getD","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L59-L73","doc":"**Row-length lookup of `removeCorner`.** For a removable corner `i` of a descending shape,\n`removeCorner λ i` has row lengths `λ` with row `i` decremented (and the vanished last row dropped). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.filter_ne_zero_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.filter_ne_zero_getD","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTCornerListConnection.lean#L30-L57","doc":"**Filtering trailing zeros preserves `getD` at every index, for a descending-sorted list.** In a\nlist sorted `≥`, the nonzero entries are a prefix, so `filter (· ≠ 0)` drops only trailing zeros and\nthe indexed lookup is unchanged (out-of-range lookups are `0` on both sides). ","signatureChunk":0}]}